## Mandatory Rules
1. Require Java 21 LTS and `<parameters>true</parameters>` in `maven-compiler-plugin`.
2. Follow the 2-Directory Contract:
   - `entity/`: JPA `@Entity` extending `BaseAuditEntity`. NEVER use `@Data` on JPA entities (`@Getter @Setter @NoArgsConstructor @AllArgsConstructor @SuperBuilder @EqualsAndHashCode(callSuper = true)`). NEVER invent `@SoftDelete` (soft-delete, UUIDv7 `id`, and `@Version` come from `BaseAuditEntity`).
   - `controller/`: `@AutoRestController` interface extending `AutoApiController<E>` or narrow interfaces (`AutoReadApi<E>`..`AutoAiApi<E>`). Do NOT write manual CRUD repositories/services/controllers for auto-managed entities.
3. Only import annotations from the 6 real packages:
   - `io.github.natswarchuan.core.annotation.*` (54)
   - `io.github.natswarchuan.module.cache.http.annotation.HttpCacheable`
   - `io.github.natswarchuan.module.datasource.annotation.{TargetDataSource, TargetDatabasePlatform}`
   - `io.github.natswarchuan.module.event.annotation.PublishCloudEvent`
   - `io.github.natswarchuan.module.lock.annotation.DistributedLock`
   - `io.github.natswarchuan.module.webhook.annotation.EntityWebhook`
4. Verified Runtime Pitfalls (NEVER Break):
   - `@StateMachine.transitions`: colon syntax `"CREATED:PENDING_PAYMENT,CANCELLED"`, NEVER `"FROM -> TO"`. Invoke transitions via `POST /api/v1/{entity}/{id}/transition?targetState=...`, NEVER JSON body.
   - Query operators: dot syntax (`retailPrice.gte=1000&productName.like=MacBook`), NEVER `__gte`.
   - CamelCase base paths: `ECommerceOrder` -> `/api/v1/e-commerce-orders` (or set explicit `basePath`).
   - Inject framework `@AutoComponent` helpers (`DynamicEntityAiMetadataProviderHelper`, `AiNaturalLanguageQueryParserHelper`, `ThirdPartyRestClientHelper`, `WebhookDispatcherHelper`) via `ObjectProvider<T>` and call `.getObject()` at runtime.
   - Consumer `@Service` beans using `@DistributedLock`, `@AutoCacheable`, `@AutoCacheEvict`, or `@TargetDataSource` MUST be non-final and `@Lazy` (class + method `@TargetDataSource` for `REPLICA` on `v0.1.0`), AND callers injecting them MUST use `ObjectProvider<MyService>` or `@Lazy`. NEVER put `@Transactional` on `public final class` Helpers.
   - Dev JWT endpoint is `POST /api/v1/auth/token?username=admin&role=ROLE_ADMIN`; `JwtTokenService.generateToken(username, userId, roles)` takes `username` FIRST.
   - Controllers with `readDto = X.class` project ALL responses through `X`; put custom DTO endpoints on a controller without `readDto`.
   - `@ServiceOverride` custom methods default to `writeRoles` (fail-closed); `@CustomEndpoint` dispatches directly to the delegated Spring bean (place security/AOP on the delegated bean).
   - Outbox event types use `EventConstant` (`ENTITY_CREATED`); `POST /api/v1/storage/upload` returns `201 Created`.
5. Production Lockdown:
   - Keep `app.framework.studio.enabled: false`, `demo-token-endpoint-enabled: false`, `fail-fast-weak-jwt-secret: true`, and `JWT_SECRET >= 32` bytes in `application.yml` / `application-prod.yml`. Enable Dev Studio only in `application-dev.yml`.
   - Protect every business entity with `@EntitySecurity(...)` and sensitive columns with `@FieldSecurity(...)`.
   - Run `mvn clean verify` (`0` failures, `0` `@Disabled`) and check `CHECKLIST.md` before completing any task.
